                <pb facs="0418" n="324" sameAs="frus:frus1930v03/pg324"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860P.512 Residence/24</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Latvia</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Coleman</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-10-28">October 28, 1930</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 772</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to the Legation’s despatch
                    No. 6960, dated May 10, 1930, the Department desires to be informed whether the
                    formal assurance of the abolition of the sojourn tax on American citizens,
                    referred to in the final sentence of the despatch, was received by the Legation.
                    If it was received, it should have been communicated <pb facs="0419" n="325"
                        xml:id="pg325"/> to the Department. If it was not received, the Legation
                    should have again taken up the matter with the Foreign Office.</p>
                <p>Very truly yours,</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State:<lb/><signed>W. R. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Castle, Jr</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
